<title>BAHRAIN: Bahrain's GIB reports record $94.5 mln net in 96.</title>
<headline>Bahrain's GIB reports record $94.5 mln net in 96.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gulf International Bank (GIB) said on Wednesday it made a record $94.5 million net profit in 1996, up 5.2 percent on a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;GIB announced net income after provisions and tax for 1996 of $94.5 million,&quot; a bank statement said. GIB posted a $89.8 million net profit in 1995.</p>
<p>It said the bank would issue its balance sheet later.</p>
<p>The Bahrain-based bank is wholly owned by Kuwait-based Gulf Investment Corp which in turn is held by the governments of Saudi Arabia, Bahrain, Oman, Qatar, Kuwait and the United Arab Emirates.</p>
